    - target: {fileID: 6380436179282662226, guid: 76354cb641cf5aa46ba4902d9b7024f7, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: '<font="bold">Amsterdam Centraal </font>station is the largest railway
        station in Amsterdam, North Holland, the Netherlands. A major international
        railway hub, it is used by 192,000 passengers a day, making it the second
        busiest railway station in the country after Utrecht Centraal and the most
        visited Rijksmonument of the Netherlands.

        <font="bold">Amsterdam
        Centraal </font>was designed by Dutch architect Pierre Cuypers and opened
        in 1889. It features a Gothic, Renaissance Revival station building and a
        cast iron platform roof spanning approximately 40 metres (130 ft). '
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
